 where his  talents lay and he did not anticipate  the scope of his own success he always  knew he can make a positive contribution  and in a different way than most by  having faith in himself Henson was able  to reinvent the world of puppetry and  enrich imaginations around the world  according to Henson the show's not dead  as long as I believe in it I think if  you study if you learn too much of what  others have done you may tend to take  the same directions everyone else it's  just a matter of figuring out how to  receive the ideas or information that  are waiting to be heard I find that it  really helped me to start the day with a  good frame of reference  as part of my prayers I think whoever's  helping me I'm sure that somebody or  something is action item number to  remain positive about your goals as  entrepreneurs we want things to happen  immediately unfortunately the world  often makes us wait hold on to your  goals and know that they are possible as  long as you have hope you think of ways  to make things work out seconds that  motivate you and that provide value to  others and don't let them go until you  reach them when you believe in them  others around you will as well an  eternal optimist Henson took uniquely  spiritual approach to his work he  believed that he was on the earth to  achieve something that would contribute  back to others as long as he tried to  create a positive message through his  work the results would be positive in  return it was this optimism that allowed  Henson to succeed even in the face of  rejection and doubt  despite the often negative response and  Henson got to his ideas he looked upon  everything as a learning experience and  a growth opportunity Henson recognized  that there would always be a certain  amount of negativity and suffering not  only in his own life but also throughout  the world however he saw little point in  wasting his energies focusing on that  instead he directed his energies towards  more constructive efforts  according to Henson I believe in taking  a positive attitude toward the world  toward people toward my work I believe  that we form our own lives that we  create our own reality and that  everything works out for the best I  think this is why we're here to work our  way through all this and hopefully come  out a bit wiser I'm better for having  gone through it all I know I drive some  people crazy with what seems to be  ridiculous optimism but it has always  worked out for me action item number  three take the road less traveled you've  got to do something different to stand  out doing the same thing as everyone  else is not a recipe for success  find out what's unique about you as an  individual and your business leverage  your uniqueness and show people how  you're different  don't try to market to everyone find  your niche provide overwhelming value  and then expand your customer base  hence it not only revolutionized  children's television around the world  but with this pioneering technology you  who brought puppetry to a higher level  his success came from being able to  devise a new way to approach an ancient  form Henson set what would become the  new standard in the industry with his  imaginative ability to think outside the  box  it was Henson's innovative and  pioneering spirit that served as major  drivers of his success he refused to  settle for the status quo and insisted  on creating something new fresh and fun  it was a risk but one that eventually  paid off The Muppets have leapt off the  television screens and become part of  families around the world according to  Henson you know that my feeling about  puppetry relates to stylization  simplicity boiling down to it's a  wonderful form and I really love it  nobody creates a fad it just happens  people love going along with the idea of  a beautiful pig it's like a conspiracy  life's like a movie write your own  ending keep believing keep pretending  simple is good  so remember remain faithful to yourself  remain positive about your goals and  take the road less traveled to finish up  this video I wanted to share one of my  favorite true stories about Jim Henson  and some of his best quotes Kermit was  not always the best-known character Jim  Henson created in fact the most popular  character originally was Rolf the doc  Henson created this Muppet for Purina  Dog Chow and it became an instant hit in  1962 long before Kermit was known to  most people not only was Rowlf the dog  more popular the character was a regular  on the Jimmy Dean show throughout 1965 a  full decade before the Muppet Show ever  aired for the first time on PBS  thank you for joining me for another  edition modeling masters if you liked  the video and you want to see more  please give it a thumbs up below I'd  also love to hear from you if you want  to leave a comment under the video I  always try to respond to all of them  that I see so please leave a comment  under the video and thank you and we'll  see you on the next episode  you
 

